! vfl_cross_special_words.strap -- VFL stores crossing into or out of
! word 11 (the indicator register), CONNECT TO MEMORY crossing into word
! 7 (the connective counters), and CM's refill path's counts.
!
! THE ORDER QUESTION, AND THE PAGES ARE NOT SILENT ON IT (Reference
! Manual 22-6530-2, read in the page images):
!   printed p.37, Indicator Register: "Bit positions 0-19 ... can be read,
!   but not loaded.  Any attempt to store into these positions has no
!   effect. ... When an instruction calls for storing into any part of the
!   indicator register, the result in bits 20-63 of the indicator register
!   will be the same as if this operation had acted upon any other storage
!   location whose initial contents were the same as those of the indicator
!   register at the start of execution of the instruction.  The setting of
!   any of the indicators 20-63 that would normally occur as part of the
!   store operation is overridden by this result."
!   printed p.76, Counts: "The counts are set at the end of the
!   connective operations, so their previous values may be used as
!   operands in the operation"; "In CONNECT TO MEMORY, the counts are made
!   on the result field after it is converted to the byte size of the
!   storage operand."  printed p.36: the left-zeros counter is bits 17-23
!   of location 7, the all-ones counter bits 44-50.
! So in word 11 the STORED WORD wins in 20-63, over every indicator the
! operation itself sets, whether word 11 is the field's first word or its
! second, and even when the field reaches only the read-only bits 0-19.
! In word 7 the COUNTS win in their two fields, being set at the end.
!
! HOW THE MODEL GETS THERE.  Word 11: writeWord(11) goes through
! StretchStorage's indStW and commitIndicators takes 20-63 from it over the
! instruction's setIndicatorBits (2026-11-16).  A crossing store's second
! word below 32 is written the NEXT clock by rl_tail_write, after the
! operation's indicators, so it overrides them too.  (For that one clock
! the operation's own indicators are in the register; with the
! interruption system enabled an indicator set there could in principle be
! seen -- not exercised, OPEN.)  Word 7: writeWord does not write the
! counter fields at all (StretchStorage's note, a documented
! simplification), so the counts always win -- which is p.76's order for a
! connective.  For ST or M+ into word 7 (p.76: the counts "are not
! changed as an inherent part of any other non-connective operations", so
! the store should land) the model DROPS the stored count bits -- a
! deviation, not an order, recorded OPEN in docs/NEXT.md and not tested.
!
! CASES (hand-derived; Z,$IND first in each C case, so word 11 starts 0):
!   C1  M+(BU,48,8) acc 1 at 10.40: the field is word 10 bits 40-63 (not
!       assigned, read 0) and word 11 bits 0-23.  0 + 1 = 1, its low bit
!       is word 11 bit 23 (PF).  The tail into 11 wins in 20-63: PF ON
!       (stored, not an overflow), and the operation's own MOP and RGZ
!       OFF.  I1 = (16)10000000000.
!   C2  M+(BU,16,8) acc 1 at 10.56: the 1 lands in word 11 bit 7,
!       read-only, no effect; the store still overrides 20-63 with the
!       initial 0.  I2 = 0 (no MOP, no RGZ).
!   C3  ST(BU,16,8) acc (16)BEEF at 11.56: HEAD in word 11 (bits 56-63 :=
!       BE), tail in word 12 bits 0-7 (the mask's permanent ones, p.37).
!       ST's MOP is overridden.  I3 = (16)BE.
!   K1  CM0101(BU,8,8) acc FF at KW1 (one word, no refill): counts of FF
!       in 8 bits, left zeros 0, ones 8.  Word 7 = 8<<13 = (16)10000.
!   K2  CM0101(V+ICR)(BU,8,8) acc 0F through X7, count 1 (the REFILL
!       path): left zeros 4, ones 4.  Word 7 = (16)40000008000.  X7 :=
!       the refill word, (16)01348000013405DC.  (Before 2026-11-17 this
!       path set no counts and word 7 stayed K1's.)
!   K3  CM0101(BU,64,8) acc (16)00F0000000000000 at 6.32: word 6 bits
!       32-63 := 00F00000, word 7 bits 0-31 := 0 (the tail).  Counts:
!       left zeros 8, ones 4.  p.76: the counts win in bits 17-23 over the
!       tail's 0.  Word 7 = (16)80000008000 (the rest of word 7 is 0
!       either way, so the full word is checked).
! CYCLES 389 is a model pin.
!
! MEASURED INJECTIONS, 2026-11-17 (in the worktree from a saved copy,
! restored and compared with cmp; observed on this deck and the other two
! new decks, which pass under all three; the rest of the suite was not
! run under them):
!   J5 CM's refill path does not hand back its counts (the old path):
!      FAIL K2 = (16)10000 (K1's counts) ONLY.
!   J6 commitIndicators ORs the operation's own indicators over the store
!      (`sv[43:0] | ind[43:0]`, the store not winning): FAIL I1 =
!      (16)10000000120, I2 = (16)120, I3 = (16)1BE -- the tail case and the
!      head case both; K1-K3 pass.  (The rest of the suite was not run
!      under J6.)
!   J7 rl_tail_write also loads the counters from a tail into word 7
!      (the tail's stored bits winning over the counts, p.76's order
!      reversed): FAIL K3 = (16)8000 ONLY.  bsc accepted it (a separate
!      rule from execute()).
! K1 and K3 are the controls for J5; K1-K3 for J6; K1, K2 for J7.
! (J5 and J6 were measured before the p.22 index-part change to
! StretchExecute.bsv, which no case of this deck reaches; J7 after it.)
!
        SLC, 1000.0
! ---- C: the indicator register (word 11) ----------------------
START   L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        M+(BU,48,8), 10.40
        TI, 1, $IND, I1
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        M+(BU,16,8), 10.56
        TI, 1, $IND, I2
        L(BU,16,8), HBEEF
        Z, $IND
        ST(BU,16,8), 11.56
        TI, 1, $IND, I3
        Z, $IND
! ---- K: the connective counts (word 7) --------------------------
        L(BU,8,8), HFF
        CM0101(BU,8,8), KW1
        TI, 1, 7, K1
        L(BU,8,8), H0F
        LX, $X7, XPK
        CM0101(V+ICR)(BU,8,8), 0($X7), 0
        TI, 1, 7, K2
        SX, $X7, K2X
        L(BU,64,8), XF0
        CM0101(BU,64,8), 6.32
        TI, 1, 7, K3
        Z, $IND
PASS    BEW, $

        SLC, 1500.0
XPK     XW, KW2, 1, RFW          ! count 1: the refill fires
RFW     XW, 1234.0, 77, 1500.0
ONE     DD(BU,64), (16)0100000000000000
HBEEF   DD(BU,64), (16)BEEF000000000000
HFF     DD(BU,64), (16)FF00000000000000
H0F     DD(BU,64), (16)0F00000000000000
XF0     DD(BU,64), (16)00F0000000000000
KW1     DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
KW2     DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5

        SLC, 1700.0
I1      DD(BU,64), 0
I2      DD(BU,64), 0
I3      DD(BU,64), 0
K1      DD(BU,64), 0
K2      DD(BU,64), 0
K2X     DD(BU,64), 0
K3      DD(BU,64), 0
        END, START
